What I can say from the evidence is that the desk also would not give HYG’s drawdown for the same attribution period. The only HYG drawdown it returned was 2.34% [f_561bc037c06e] over 2026-02-20 to 2026-03-27, and its window return was 3.17% [f_aba85a9fa6a0] over 2025-09-10 to 2026-09-10. Those are not the same period as the latest run attribution, so I cannot use them to say whether HYG’s own drawdown matches the sign of its contribution.

So the answer for the book is: the reconciliation gap is not available from the desk, the largest and smallest contributing factors are not available, and the HYG sign check is not supportable with the evidence returned. If you want, I can try again by asking the desk specifically for the latest run’s attribution table and the matching HYG period."}

